WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.153
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.453 --> 00:00:09.118
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.418 --> 00:00:16.703
Unit thirteen: Security Studies. Today you will describe widening concepts using expand to include / broaden to cover.

4
00:00:17.003 --> 00:00:19.713
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:24.062
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.917 --> 00:00:26.510
National security.

7
00:00:27.517 --> 00:00:31.989
National security means the protection of a state and its citizens from threats.

8
00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:36.057
National security once meant only military defence.

9
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.802
Your turn. Say: National security.

10
00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.062
National security.

11
00:00:44.817 --> 00:00:45.899
Deterrence.

12
00:00:46.883 --> 00:00:51.193
Deterrence means discouraging an attack by threatening unacceptable retaliation.

13
00:00:51.783 --> 00:00:54.851
Nuclear deterrence depends on credible response.

14
00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.033
Your turn. Say: Deterrence.

15
00:01:00.867 --> 00:01:01.868
Deterrence.

16
00:01:02.617 --> 00:01:03.908
Nonproliferation.

17
00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:08.426
Nonproliferation means efforts to stop the spread of weapons.

18
00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:12.026
Nonproliferation treaties limit nuclear arsenals.

19
00:01:12.617 --> 00:01:15.408
Your turn. Say: Nonproliferation.

20
00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:19.790
Nonproliferation.

21
00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.097
Asymmetric warfare.

22
00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:27.335
Asymmetric warfare means conflict between sides of very unequal strength.

23
00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.983
Asymmetric warfare favours surprise and mobility.

24
00:01:31.583 --> 00:01:34.363
Your turn. Say: Asymmetric warfare.

25
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.816
Asymmetric warfare.

26
00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:40.957
Cybersecurity.

27
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:45.877
Cybersecurity means protection of computer systems from attack.

28
00:01:46.483 --> 00:01:49.597
Cybersecurity now protects hospitals and grids.

29
00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:53.602
Your turn. Say: Cybersecurity.

30
00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:57.828
Cybersecurity.

31
00:01:58.583 --> 00:01:59.863
Intelligence.

32
00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:04.359
Intelligence means information gathered about threats and rivals.

33
00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.170
Good intelligence prevented the attack.

34
00:02:07.783 --> 00:02:10.296
Your turn. Say: Intelligence.

35
00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.460
Intelligence.

36
00:02:15.217 --> 00:02:16.659
Collective security.

37
00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.937
Collective security means an arrangement where all states act against an aggressor.

38
00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:25.258
Collective security underpinned the UN Charter.

39
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:29.129
Your turn. Say: Collective security.

40
00:02:31.967 --> 00:02:33.699
Collective security.

41
00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:36.124
Strategic stability.

42
00:02:37.117 --> 00:02:41.879
Strategic stability means a condition in which no side gains by striking first.

43
00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:46.039
Arms control aims to preserve strategic stability.

44
00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.500
Your turn. Say: Strategic stability.

45
00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:54.170
Strategic stability.

46
00:02:54.967 --> 00:02:58.536
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:59.383 --> 00:03:04.311
Visal, my father says security means soldiers and borders. Is that all it means now?

48
00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:12.365
Not any more. Security has expanded to include cyber threats, pandemics and climate shocks.

49
00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:15.217
Why did the definition change?

50
00:03:16.317 --> 00:03:26.179
Because threats have broadened to cover non-military risks. A power-grid failure can harm more people than a small raid.

51
00:03:27.283 --> 00:03:29.167
Does that make policy harder?

52
00:03:30.283 --> 00:03:41.864
Yes. Collective security must now extend to include shared digital infrastructure, and deterrence must adapt to anonymous attackers.

53
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.756
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:45.617 --> 00:03:49.369
Grammar focus: Expand to include and broaden to cover.

55
00:03:49.669 --> 00:03:50.787
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:51.483 --> 00:03:54.470
Security has expanded to include cyber threats.

57
00:03:55.383 --> 00:03:58.997
The agenda has broadened to cover pandemics and climate shocks.

58
00:03:59.883 --> 00:04:04.275
Collective security must extend to include digital infrastructure.

59
00:04:05.233 --> 00:04:13.586
expand / broaden / extend + to + include / cover + new items. Use the present perfect for a change that continues to the present: has expanded.

60
00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:19.440
Be careful! Don't say: Security expanded include cyber threats.

61
00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.466
Say: Security has expanded to include cyber threats.

62
00:04:25.766 --> 00:04:27.348
expand to include.

63
00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:30.786
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.402
A Wider Idea of Safety.

65
00:04:33.702 --> 00:04:39.115
Traditional security studies focused on states, armies and the balance of military power.

66
00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:47.382
Cold War strategy relied on deterrence and nonproliferation to maintain strategic stability between nuclear rivals.

67
00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:54.511
Since then, the concept has expanded to include terrorism, cyberattacks, pandemics and climate change.

68
00:04:55.500 --> 00:05:02.631
Asymmetric warfare allows weaker actors to challenge stronger ones, and attribution of cyberattacks is often unclear.

69
00:05:03.633 --> 00:05:10.323
Collective security arrangements must therefore adapt, because no single state can defend against every modern threat.

70
00:05:11.433 --> 00:05:15.470
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:16.317 --> 00:05:19.593
Security has expanded blank include cyber threats.

72
00:05:19.893 --> 00:05:22.850
A, to. B, for. C, of.

73
00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.005
The answer is A: to.

74
00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:32.380
Discouraging attack by threatening retaliation is blank.

75
00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:37.262
A, deterrence. B, intelligence. C, nonproliferation.

76
00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.591
The answer is A: deterrence.

77
00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.191
Efforts to stop the spread of weapons are blank.

78
00:05:46.491 --> 00:05:51.479
A, asymmetric warfare. B, nonproliferation. C, stability.

79
00:05:55.033 --> 00:05:57.811
The answer is B: nonproliferation.

80
00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.729
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:06:01.029 --> 00:06:08.966
A, Threats have broadened to cover pandemics.. B, Threats have broadened cover pandemics.. C, Threats have broaden to cover pandemics..

82
00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:16.148
The answer is A: Threats have broadened to cover pandemics..

83
00:06:17.283 --> 00:06:20.200
According to the reading, no single state can…

84
00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:26.603
A, defend against every modern threat. B, build weapons. C, join treaties.

85
00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:33.803
The answer is A: defend against every modern threat.

86
00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.105
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:42.494
How has the definition of 'security' expanded in the modern era?

88
00:06:59.283 --> 00:07:00.668
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:00.968 --> 00:07:26.636
Security has expanded from protecting borders to protecting people and systems. It now includes cyber defence, public health, food and energy supply, and climate resilience. A pandemic or a cyberattack on a power grid can cause as much harm as a conventional attack. As a result, governments must cooperate across agencies and across borders.

90
00:07:26.936 --> 00:07:28.785
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:29.683 --> 00:07:34.588
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and expand to include and broaden to cover.

92
00:07:34.888 --> 00:07:40.826
Today's value is global security awareness. Understand that peace depends on many kinds of safety.

93
00:07:41.126 --> 00:07:43.894
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

94
00:07:44.194 --> 00:07:47.067
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

